;; A death test for cleanup safety, not for the refusal itself: a LATER
;; execute argument carrying an embedded NUL used to raise past the argv
;; vector and every argument copied before it -- 29 bytes definitely lost
;; under the Valgrind lane. The refusal message is io-nul-pattern.fe's;
;; what is pinned here is that nothing is left behind on the way out.
(execute "true" "a\0b")
(print "not reached")
